      "dom_id": "step-q331948",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=$ {{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{2{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=2L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+3L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-4=2{X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-3=-{X}_{1}(s)+3{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-2){X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s)=4 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-3){X}_{2}(s)=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-2)[3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s)]+2{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ 3(s-2)-[(s-2)(s-3)-2]{X}_{2}(s) & =4 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s+4){X}_{2}(s) & =4-3(s-2) \\\\ -(s-1)(s-4){X}_{2}(s) & =-3s+10 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =3-(s-3){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =3-(s-3)\\cdot \\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(s-1)(s-4)-(s-3)(3s-10)}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s-18}{(s-1)(s-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-9)}{(s-1)(s-4)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{3s-10}{(s-1)(s-4)}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
