      "source_example_id": "e-21155",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Solution of a Laplace Transformed Initial Value Problem",
      "kp_id": "e-21155"
    },
    "q-332038": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332038",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform $L$ to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a system with variables ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$ In terms of the parameter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the Laplace transforms of both sides of each equation in our system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}L\\{{x}_{1}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ L\\{{x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\}=L\\{-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\n$$\n\nUsing the derivative property of the Laplace transform, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}sL\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}-{x}_{1}(0)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+2L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\} \\\\ sL\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}-{x}_{2}(0)=-L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}+4L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich can be simplified to the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s{X}_{1}(s)-3={X}_{1}(s)+2{X}_{2}(s) \\\\ s{X}_{2}(s)-2=-{X}_{1}(s)+4{X}_{2}(s)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}$ and ${X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}.$\n\nRewriting the system in standard form, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(s-1){X}_{1}(s)-2{X}_{2}(s)=3 \\\\ {X}_{1}(s)+(s-4){X}_{2}(s)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from the second equation, we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(s-1)[2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s)]-2{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ 2(s-1)-[(s-1)(s-4)+2]{X}_{2}(s) & =3 \\\\ -({s}^{2}-5s+6){X}_{2}(s) & =3-2(s-1) \\\\ -(s-2)(s-3){X}_{2}(s) & =-2s+5 \\\\ {X}_{2}(s) & =\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find ${X}_{1}(s):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{X}_{1}(s) & =2-(s-4){X}_{2}(s) \\\\  & =2-(s-4)\\cdot \\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(s-2)(s-3)-(s-4)(2s-5)}{(s-2)(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{3s-8}{(s-2)(s-3)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=\\frac{2s-5}{(s-2)(s-3)}.\n$$",
