    "q-332438": {
      "dom_id": "step-q332438",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=4{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\,x(0)=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{4}{5s}+\\frac{41}{5(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=\\frac{16}{5s}-\\frac{41}{5(s-5)}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n$x(t)=\\,\\,$\n</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n$\\,\\,+\\,\\,$\n</td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n\n<td rowspan=\"2\" height=\"40px\" align=\"center\">\n$\\,\\,{e}^{5t}$\n</td>\n\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td></td>\n\n<td width=\"5px\" height=\"30px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td></td>\n\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>",
      "worked_solution": "To find ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ satisfying the original initial value problem, we apply the inverse Laplace transform to ${X}_{1}(s)$ and ${X}_{2}(s)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{1}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{4}{5s}+\\frac{41}{5(s-5)}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\,{L}^{-1}\\,\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}\\,+\\,\\frac{41}{5}\\,{L}^{-1}\\,\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{41}{5}{e}^{5t} \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={L}^{-1}\\{{X}_{2}(s)\\} \\\\  & ={L}^{-1}\\{\\frac{16}{5s}-\\frac{41}{5(s-5)}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}{L}^{-1}\\,\\{\\frac{1}{s}\\}\\,-\\,\\frac{41}{5}\\,{L}^{-1}\\,\\{\\frac{1}{s-5}\\} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{5}-\\frac{41}{5}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\nx(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{41}{5}{e}^{5t} \\\\ \\frac{16}{5}-\\frac{41}{5}{e}^{5t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{41}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{41}{5}\\end{aligned}]{e}^{5t}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
